#: ../../library/numbers.rst:123
msgid "Implementing the arithmetic operations"
msgstr "Die arithmetischen Operationen umsetzen"

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:125
msgid ""
"We want to implement the arithmetic operations so that mixed-mode operations "
"either call an implementation whose author knew about the types of both "
"arguments, or convert both to the nearest built in type and do the operation "
"there. For subtypes of :class:`Integral`, this means "
"that :meth:`~object.__add__` and :meth:`~object.__radd__` should be defined "
"as::"
msgstr ""
"Die arithmetischen Operationen sollen so umgesetzt werden, dass Operationen "
"mit gemischten Typen entweder eine Implementierung aufrufen, deren Autor die "
"Typen beider Argumente kannte, oder beide in den nächstgelegenen "
"integrierten Typ umwandeln und die Operation dort ausführen. Für Untertypen "
"von :class:`Integral` heißt das, dass :meth:`~object.__add__` "
"und :meth:`~object.__radd__` so definiert werden sollten::"

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:157
msgid ""
"There are 5 different cases for a mixed-type operation on subclasses "
"of :class:`Complex`. I'll refer to all of the above code that doesn't refer "
"to ``MyIntegral`` and ``OtherTypeIKnowAbout`` as \"boilerplate\". ``a`` will "
"be an instance of ``A``, which is a subtype of :class:`Complex` (``a : A <: "
"Complex``), and ``b : B <: Complex``. I'll consider ``a + b``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:164
msgid ""
"If ``A`` defines an :meth:`~object.__add__` which accepts ``b``, all is well."
msgstr ""
"Definiert ``A`` ein :meth:`~object.__add__`, das ``b`` annimmt, ist alles in "
"Ordnung."

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:166
msgid ""
"If ``A`` falls back to the boilerplate code, and it were to return a value "
"from :meth:`~object.__add__`, we'd miss the possibility that ``B`` defines a "
"more intelligent :meth:`~object.__radd__`, so the boilerplate should "
"return :data:`NotImplemented` from :meth:`!__add__`. (Or ``A`` may not "
"implement :meth:`!__add__` at all.)"
msgstr ""
"Fällt ``A`` auf den Boilerplate-Code zurück und würde dieser einen Wert "
"aus :meth:`~object.__add__` zurückgeben, entginge uns die Möglichkeit, dass "
"``B`` ein klügeres :meth:`~object.__radd__` definiert. Der Boilerplate-Code "
"sollte deshalb :data:`NotImplemented` aus :meth:`!__add__` zurückgeben. "
"(Oder ``A`` setzt :meth:`!__add__` gar nicht um.)"

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:172
msgid ""
"Then ``B``'s :meth:`~object.__radd__` gets a chance. If it accepts ``a``, "
"all is well."
msgstr ""
"Dann kommt das :meth:`~object.__radd__` von ``B`` zum Zug. Nimmt es ``a`` "
"an, ist alles in Ordnung."

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:174
msgid ""
"If it falls back to the boilerplate, there are no more possible methods to "
"try, so this is where the default implementation should live."
msgstr ""
"Fällt es auf den Boilerplate-Code zurück, gibt es keine weiteren Methoden "
"zum Ausprobieren. Hier gehört deshalb die Standardimplementierung hin."

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:177
msgid ""
"If ``B <: A``, Python tries ``B.__radd__`` before ``A.__add__``. This is ok, "
"because it was implemented with knowledge of ``A``, so it can handle those "
"instances before delegating to :class:`Complex`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../library/numbers.rst:182
msgid ""
"If ``A <: Complex`` and ``B <: Real`` without sharing any other knowledge, "
"then the appropriate shared operation is the one involving the built "
"in :class:`complex`, and both :meth:`~object.__radd__` s land there, so "
"``a+b == b+a``."
msgstr ""

